WEBVTT

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.330
Long ago, a demon appeared on the outskirts of a village.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.830
The demon wasn't in good health, so a young lad from the village fed him.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:29.840
The demon recovered its strength, and remained in the village to play with the young lad.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:36.640
Because of the demon, the villagers forgot to work and spent their days in leisure.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.520
One day, an exorcist appeared, and sealed away the demon.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.940
Although the demon was taken care of,

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:54.320
the village wasted away because the villagers had forgotten all about it.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.030
Thus, future generations held a celebration every eleven years to honor

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:07.080
the exorcism of this demon in order not to forget what happened to that village.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.180
Was that the beginning?

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.180
Yeah, it's a story from a thousand years ago.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.350
By the way, if it were you guys, what would you do?

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:29.610
If you met the demon from this picture book, what would you do?

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:48.250
Crap! I even set five different alarms!

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.630
You guys are in my way. Move!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.270
That was a pretty bad fall for an adult!

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.520
Oh, no! This guy's nose is smashed!

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.230
Does it hurt? Are you gonna cry?

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.860
You kids think it's all right to be prowling around this late at night?

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.660
Go home this instant!

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.580
Making an adult angry is scary! Get that in your heads!

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:36.340
Hi-yu-mu... Festival?

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.200
Damn it!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.410
They're out there having fun while we have to work.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.910
Shura-san! Watch your head!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.160
Ah?!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.420
It sure is low.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:59.420
All the sluice gates are closed for the festival, so the water level is higher than usual.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.180
Over here?

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.020
True Cross Academy: Sluice Gate No. 1.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.650
Well, we're finally here. You need to help out too.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:37.880
The Phantom Train is, um, a train possessed by a demon,

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.880
that is heading towards Gehenna from Assiah.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.010
He's late! What on earth is he doing?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.550
Also known as the Man-Eating Train.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.390
The correct name is the Soul-Eating Train.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.850
You've studied really hard for this, Shiemi-san.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.480
It's here.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.980
That's our exorcism target this time: the Phantom Train.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:07.280
Lord Pheles has restored the ancient ruins that were originally buried here

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.620
There are twenty-eight such places surrounding the town.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.750
Every eleven years, the seals have to be reactivated to protect the town from demons.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.710
This year is exactly eleven years from the last time we did this, so—

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.300
Spare us the explanation.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.050
Pick one.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.300
Oh, yeah!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.850
You'll be in charge of activating the new barrier.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.720
And I'll deactivate the old one.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.560
Let's get this over with quickly and go grab a drink!

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:06.720
Shiemi-san.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.550
Please be careful.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.600
The demon waits for this kind of opportunity and drags the unfortunate passenger to Gehenna.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.980
We'll be riding this one.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.940
But there are people inside.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.410
They are the ghosts of the people who boarded the train.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.780
They probably haven't even realized that they're dead.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.700
No way... We have to help them!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.250
It's impossible.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:37.960
What?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:42.080
Once we exorcise the Phantom Train, the ghosts inside will disappear as well.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:48.300
It's unfortunate, but I'm afraid we don't have time to help the ghosts this time.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.020
Is this a tool for exorcism too?

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.310
This is a special car prepared specifically for this mission.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.410
Rin still isn't here.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.540
Can't do anything about it. This mission will have to be carried out by the two of us—

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.290
He's here!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.790
Rin, over here!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.540
Shiemi! Hold on! Wait up!

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.340
Nii-san!

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.340
Hurry up!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.380
Keep at it! Just a little more!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.020
What on earth were you thinking, being late for a mission?!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.030
Do you really want to be an exorcist, Nii-san?!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.200
I poured my heart into studying.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.870
That's why I fell asleep...

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.910
Anyway, I'm sorry.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.370
But I made it, so it's not a big deal, right? Stop nagging me.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.000
More importantly, we should exorcise this thing quickly.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:02.870
Rin, don't!

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.790
It hurts!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.050
Seriously. You never listen to what others are saying.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.180
Well then, I'll explain today's mission.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.970
It is 11:50 right now.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.680
You two will stay in the railcar and wait.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.440
I will go to the front car by myself.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:31.740
At exactly midnight, the Phantom Train will reveal its true from in order to return to Gehenna.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.650
I'll exorcise it when it transforms.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:43.040
After the exorcism, you two will pull the brakes on the railcar and stop the train.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.670
After we have safely stopped the train, we'll wait for the Recovery Squad to come and get us.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.880
And that will be the end of this mission.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.470
What the hell? So we're only here to pull the brakes?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.850
However, if I am unable to exorcise the train, we'll all be headed for Gehenna.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:07.730
And if I were to fail, press that red button to separate the rail car from the train.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.610
Then, pull the brakes and make your escape.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.780
And what will you do?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.780
Forget about me and focus on your part of the mission.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.920
That bastard's acting all cool.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.500
Rin! There are ghosts inside.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:38.590
Yuki-chan said we don't have time for them, but I wonder if we can help them.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.350
Is there a way that we can help them?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.350
We might be able to if we use the Japanese Lantern Plant.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.270
It has the power to gather spirits.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.650
Although we won't know until we try.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.530
Got it. Leave it to me!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.840
Well then, we'll proceed as discussed.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.590
Understood.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:54.000
He's doing pretty well.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.630
Well then, I should get started too!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.390
Let's get goin'.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.210
Can you do it, Shiemi?

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:34.790
Nii-chan.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.350
The color, shape and scent of the Japanese Lantern Plant,

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:55.110
written as the "Ghost Light", bestows upon it the power to summon ghosts.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.820
That's what my grandma told me.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.470
Five more minutes.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.140
Yukio!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:34.940
Wait up a bit.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.810
Shiemi's helping the ghosts right now.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.610
What on earth are you doing, Nii-san?!

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.440
Those people are still alive!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.950
We need to hold a proper memorial for them.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.200
That is completely unnecessary!

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.780
It's not unnecessary!

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.530
We're helping people!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.870
Helping people is not our job!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.160
An exorcist's job is to exorcise demons!

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.910
You're wrong, four-eyes! An exorcist's job is to help others!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:40.460
Yukio!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.460
It's still early.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.920
This is happening because you did something unnecessary!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.610
All right! We're done!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.690
It really is faster with two people.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.660
Hey, if you're free tomorrow, let's hang out.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.910
Even without asking me, I'm sure there are other excellent people from the Japanese Branch.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:15.830
I was joking.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.160
The twins...

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:20.880
I've heard the older one has powers that could frighten even Satan.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:25.590
That's just a rumor. It's nothing worth mentioning. He's still an Exwire.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.050
An Exwire?

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.590
You'd be surprised if you met him.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.230
I found a nice place nearby.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:38.440
It'll be my treat!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.560
Hey, let's take the boat to District Three—

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:43.980
Who's in charge?

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.990
Okumura-sensei and two Exwires.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.780
What the hell are they doing?!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.740
Okumura? The aforementioned twins?

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.710
What the hell is this?!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:04.250
It's getting violent because the ghosts were taken away from it!

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:07.760
Rin, I'm done here!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.760
Yuki-chan!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.470
This is an emergency. Let's hurry back to the railcar!

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:19.520
Nii-san, you hurry up too!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.230
What're you doing? Run—

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.120
He said to hurry, but at this rate...

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.330
I guess I just gotta cut this thing down.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.960
You bastard!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.490
Thirty more seconds!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.080
Run!

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.000
Nii-chan!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.290
Damn it!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.680
Yuki-chan, your arm...!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.810
What on earth are you doing, Nii-san!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:29.900
You bastard!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.710
Yukio!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.200
Hey! Are you all right?

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.990
Hang in there!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.580
Hey.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.960
Can you here me? Hang in there!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.420
Hey! Don't fall asleep! Open your eyes!

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:13.980
Shura?

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.440
Ah... This guy needs help!

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.030
So you're the spawn of Satan.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.830
Tsk. It got away

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:42.760
Yuki-chan.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.260
Hang in there, Yuki-chan!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.600
Yuki-chan!

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.730
Sancho-san: Aloe, Chorogi: Chinese Artichoke.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.730
Nii-chan, get me Sancho-san and Chorogi!

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:54.270
I'll treat you immediately, so just hold on,

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.690
Yuki-chan!

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.740
Three kilometers of road destroyed,

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.200
three buildings under reconstruction,

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.200
fifteen cars,

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.700
three sets of construction equipment, et cetera.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.460
Fortunately, there were only two casualties.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:19.210
Okumura-sensei, as the person in charge of this mission...

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:23.260
I am responsible for all this. I am very sorry.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.130
No! That was my...

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.720
Be silent, Nii-san!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.720
Lord Pheles, what are their sentences?

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.720
That's right.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:32.470
How about...

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.730
Judgment has been passed.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.240
Okumura Yukio, you are to write a full report on this.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:48.240
Okumura Rin and Moriyama Shiemi, you both are sentenced to five days of house arrest.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:51.580
Submit your written apologies by tomorrow.

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.240
Dismissed!

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:58.750
Okumura-sensei, it is unfortunate to see a spot on your fledgling career.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:07.090
Yukio...

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:10.470
Helping people is an exorcist's job, isn't it?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:16.480
To help ghosts who are dead, you would put those who are alive in danger?

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:22.070
You can't remain an Exwire forever.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:26.780
Even if you become an exorcist, your way of doing things cannot be applied.

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:31.870
Enter the check for the mutual link.

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:32.490
Okay.

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:35.250
At present...

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.750
Thank you very much.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.040
Do take care.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:42.460
Shiemi...

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.000
Were you waiting for me?

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:47.510
It's not a big deal. I'm all right.

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:50.050
Sorry. Because of me...

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:51.760
I'm really fine, and...

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:53.720
It was kinda my fault too.

00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:55.680
Hey, brat!

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.770
You brat, what was with that mess?!

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:03.980
Can't you do things properly, huh?!

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:05.480
What a joke.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:10.240
That whole incident with the Phantom Train really disappointed me.

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:12.240
You're that guy from the boat...

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.240
Oh, you guys haven't been introduced yet.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:20.290
This is Liu Seiryu, Upper First Class Exorcist from the Taiwan Branch of the Order of the True Cross.

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:22.670
What?! Hey!

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:25.000
What's going on?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.420
He was asleep on the bed but, the moment he woke up he suddenly...

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:30.680
Ow! That hurts!

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.540
Hey, calm down.

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:12.090
Hey! You're going too far. He's just a kid...

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:12.590
Look.

00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:16.810
A tail?

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:20.560
What's an exorcist doing helping a demon? Are you stupid?

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.810
Bring a cage!

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.230
An unidentified demon, huh?

00:24:27.820 --> 00:24:31.780
We found the small shrine at which it was thought to have been sealed, but there aren't any records.

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:34.820
And even if we wanted to search for it, it's buried under all that rubble.

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:37.740
I see.

00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:39.660
So, shall we kill it?

00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:41.910
What? There's no need to go that far.

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:44.750
It's the festival season now.

00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:49.130
We don't have enough manpower to find that demon's background and reseal it.

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:53.550
It'd be good if we had somebody who, even while under house arrest, is free enough to care for it.

00:24:53.550 --> 00:24:55.720
But we simply don't have such luck—

00:24:58.850 --> 00:25:01.810
Ah! I've thought of something!

00:25:02.480 --> 00:25:06.230
Okumura Rin, how about you look after it?

00:25:06.230 --> 00:25:07.940
Eh...? Why me...

00:25:07.940 --> 00:25:09.690
You were the one who brought it here in the first place.

00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:13.360
But if you can't do it, then we'll just have to dispose of it.

00:25:12.860 --> 00:25:14.740
Fine, I'll do it.

00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:16.160
What? Nii-san!

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:18.580
It's a deal.

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:21.790
Well then, here's the key for the cage.

00:25:21.790 --> 00:25:24.370
If you find that it's too much trouble, feel free to say so.

00:25:24.370 --> 00:25:26.670
I'll dispose of it immediately.

00:25:35.220 --> 00:25:37.640
Why did you say you would do it, Nii-san!

00:25:37.640 --> 00:25:39.010
I didn't have a choice.

00:25:39.010 --> 00:25:39.970
Shiemi-san.

00:25:40.850 --> 00:25:42.970
Rin! Do you have a minute?

00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:43.030
We managed to help them thanks to you, Rin.

00:26:44.660 --> 00:26:45.790
Thank you.

00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:48.960
H-How did this get in here?

00:26:50.330 --> 00:26:51.630
Here, take this.

00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:56.170
I've written down your schedule for this period of house arrest.

00:26:56.840 --> 00:26:59.340
Cleaning, taking out the trash, winter vacation homework.

00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:00.720
Make sure you do them properly!

00:27:00.720 --> 00:27:02.430
Well then, I'll be heading out.

00:27:29.660 --> 00:27:31.880
Crap! I fell asleep again!

00:27:45.470 --> 00:27:46.930
You must be thirsty.

00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:13.790
Hold it! Don't do it in there!

00:28:17.630 --> 00:28:19.210
Made it...

00:28:23.010 --> 00:28:24.510
It really stinks!

00:28:24.510 --> 00:28:27.970
Like dirty mops and old man's socks.

00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:30.810
How rude! What do you mean by "stinks"?!

00:28:32.230 --> 00:28:33.560
You can talk?

00:28:53.870 --> 00:28:55.750
Is anyone here?

00:28:55.750 --> 00:28:56.920
What's the problem?

00:28:57.340 --> 00:29:00.300
There seem to be reports regarding some supernatural activity going on here.

00:29:00.300 --> 00:29:02.260
They're so carefree.

00:29:02.260 --> 00:29:04.430
If it were me, I would've burned down the building.

00:29:04.430 --> 00:29:06.010
That's kinda violent...

00:29:06.010 --> 00:29:07.350
I was kidding.

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:08.350
Have you seen the report?

00:29:09.180 --> 00:29:13.390
The front of the Phantom Train that was torn off has been spotted under a structure in the industrial area.

00:29:13.770 --> 00:29:18.190
The main body that escaped is on the move while eating away at the boundary between Assiah and Gehenna,

00:29:18.190 --> 00:29:20.360
and is suspected to be hiding on the academy grounds.

00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:24.200
So, gaps that are weakening the barrier have been created.

00:29:26.660 --> 00:29:29.080
We've let a really troublesome guy get away.

00:29:50.510 --> 00:29:51.260
Damn it!

00:30:01.320 --> 00:30:03.230
What're you guys doing slacking around?

00:30:03.230 --> 00:30:05.280
And you call yourselves exorcists?!

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:17.420
I guess you're pretty useful.

00:30:25.090 --> 00:30:27.090
I can't do it anymore... I'm gonna die.

00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:29.430
I've lost all my confidence on the first day.

00:30:29.930 --> 00:30:32.970
Quit complaining. This is training too.

00:30:32.970 --> 00:30:35.890
Those MOLBs were amazing.

00:30:37.810 --> 00:30:39.310
Okumura, are you here?

00:30:39.310 --> 00:30:40.770
We've come to borrow your bath...

00:30:39.850 --> 00:30:41.730
Hey, behave, will ya?!

00:30:45.490 --> 00:30:46.610
"Mephi-Shampoo"?

00:30:46.610 --> 00:30:50.410
"Capture that girl with this charming sparkling essence."

00:30:50.410 --> 00:30:52.530
Do you really use this?

00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:55.500
Mephisto just left it here!

00:30:55.500 --> 00:30:56.660
Ow!

00:30:56.660 --> 00:30:58.620
Hey, it went over there.

00:31:00.460 --> 00:31:01.670
I caught it!

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.670
Wash it now!

00:31:07.800 --> 00:31:11.180
Ears? Or horns?

00:31:12.600 --> 00:31:14.180
It's kinda prickly.

00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:17.060
Kamiki-san picked this just for you.

00:31:17.060 --> 00:31:19.480
Thank you! It looks good!

00:31:19.480 --> 00:31:22.860
I didn't have enough time, so I just grabbed whatever looked suitable.

00:31:25.230 --> 00:31:26.690
Hey, it's time to get back.

00:31:27.610 --> 00:31:29.200
Ah, already?

00:31:30.990 --> 00:31:35.370
In the end, just using the bath took up all of our break time.

00:31:35.370 --> 00:31:36.450
Sorry for taking up your time.

00:31:36.790 --> 00:31:38.200
Well, we'd do the same if you were in a pinch.

00:31:38.790 --> 00:31:39.620
Let's go.

00:31:39.620 --> 00:31:41.210
We'll come to use your bath again.

00:31:51.220 --> 00:31:53.090
Oh? Where's the kid?

00:31:53.510 --> 00:31:54.930
Shit! That brat!

00:31:55.810 --> 00:31:57.470
Where the heck did he go?!

00:32:02.730 --> 00:32:04.900
Did you forget again?

00:32:04.900 --> 00:32:06.270
I remembered up until just now though!

00:32:19.660 --> 00:32:21.250
...and that concludes it.

00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:23.880
Next, the Minister of Defence...

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:46.230
Kuro!

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:47.320
Rin!

00:32:47.820 --> 00:32:51.490
Have you seen a rather small kid with a weird hairstyle around?

00:33:00.330 --> 00:33:01.330
It's him...

00:33:05.370 --> 00:33:06.500
Ah...!

00:33:07.630 --> 00:33:09.590
Rin! I got him!

00:33:11.170 --> 00:33:11.920
Here.

00:33:19.350 --> 00:33:20.720
Shall we eat?

00:33:21.020 --> 00:33:23.480
Yes, this is the Japan Branch of the Order of the True Cross.

00:33:23.480 --> 00:33:25.100
We're heading over now!

00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:26.730
There's a ghoul in District 3!

00:33:27.730 --> 00:33:32.780
The party from New Delhi will be late, so can we get everyone from the Kyoto Branch to help?

00:33:32.780 --> 00:33:36.030
We'll crush these Tokyo demons.

00:33:36.030 --> 00:33:38.740
I wonder if Renzo's doing his job properly...

00:33:44.660 --> 00:33:47.380
My older brothers should be here already...

00:33:47.380 --> 00:33:49.710
Okumura-kun sure is working hard, isn't he?

00:33:49.710 --> 00:33:51.920
Well, he's supposed to be guarding that demon.

00:33:51.920 --> 00:33:54.260
Is it even okay to give it that much freedom?

00:34:11.900 --> 00:34:13.110
Looks delicious!

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.450
It's the Super Yellow Okumura Rin special!

00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:22.080
Wanna give it a try?

00:34:22.080 --> 00:34:24.000
Thank you for the food!

00:34:34.420 --> 00:34:36.380
It melts in your mouth~

00:34:49.230 --> 00:34:51.150
It melts in my mouth~

00:34:51.520 --> 00:34:52.480
I know, right?

00:34:52.900 --> 00:34:53.940
It melts in your mouth!

00:34:56.110 --> 00:34:57.190
Thank you for the food!

00:34:59.990 --> 00:35:01.410
Thank you for the food!

00:35:12.500 --> 00:35:13.840
It melts in my mouth~

00:35:14.210 --> 00:35:16.510
Speaking of that, I haven't got your name.

00:35:16.510 --> 00:35:18.380
I'm Rin. You are?

00:35:19.550 --> 00:35:21.180
I don't have a name.

00:35:21.180 --> 00:35:24.100
Is that so? Well then, we gotta think one up for you.

00:35:24.430 --> 00:35:26.970
Maro... Usamaro...

00:35:27.310 --> 00:35:28.600
It melted in my mouth!

00:35:29.190 --> 00:35:31.190
You're done already?

00:35:31.190 --> 00:35:34.270
You gotta chew properly, Usamaro.

00:35:34.900 --> 00:35:36.480
It'll melt in my mouth!

00:35:37.150 --> 00:35:38.280
Thank you for the food!

00:35:49.290 --> 00:35:51.750
Hey, Miss! More beer!

00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:55.630
TL Note: Negima refers to alternating spring onions and chicken grilled on a stick. Mentai jaga bata is steamed potatoes with butter and marinated pollock roe.

00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:55.630
And some negima and mentai jaga bata!

00:35:55.630 --> 00:35:58.050
You sure can drink, lady!

00:35:58.050 --> 00:35:59.550
This is on the house!

00:35:59.550 --> 00:36:02.180
Sweet! You're the best!

00:36:02.180 --> 00:36:05.100
Shura-san, we're still in the middle of our mission!

00:36:05.100 --> 00:36:06.850
Quit saying such stuffy things!

00:36:07.770 --> 00:36:09.770
We're just taking a break.

00:36:09.770 --> 00:36:13.440
I can't overlook drinking while on the job, Kirigakure Shura.

00:36:13.440 --> 00:36:13.900
Wha...

00:36:14.980 --> 00:36:17.480
Mr. Arthur Auguste Angel!

00:36:18.070 --> 00:36:20.030
What's the Paladin doing here?

00:36:21.110 --> 00:36:23.910
I was asked to play the lead role in this year's festival.

00:36:23.910 --> 00:36:28.290
This refers to someone who is born in a year with the same Chinese Zodiac sign as the current year.

00:36:23.910 --> 00:36:25.910
Oh! It's the man of the year!

00:36:25.910 --> 00:36:28.290
He's finally here!

00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:34.960
Really, what're you doing, baldy?

00:36:35.630 --> 00:36:39.630
"The traces of a nostalgic festival orchestra,

00:36:39.630 --> 00:36:42.630
I ponder about the season of white snow."

00:36:42.630 --> 00:36:45.640
Cool! I wanna go to the festival too.

00:36:45.640 --> 00:36:47.300
But in this form...

00:36:47.300 --> 00:36:50.890
That can't be helped. We're laying low here.

00:36:50.890 --> 00:36:51.640
Well then!

00:36:52.180 --> 00:36:53.310
Hooray!

00:36:58.360 --> 00:36:59.230
We've got orders!

00:36:59.230 --> 00:37:01.780
There's been a sighting three hundred meters south. They're leading it here now.

00:37:01.780 --> 00:37:03.280
Bon! Did you see?

00:37:03.610 --> 00:37:05.530
It's Lena-san from Jakarta!

00:37:05.530 --> 00:37:07.410
She's totally my type!

00:37:07.740 --> 00:37:09.370
It's coming!

00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:11.000
A MOLB!

00:37:22.010 --> 00:37:23.630
Stick insects...!

00:37:23.630 --> 00:37:26.180
Not gonna happen. It just won't work out.

00:37:26.180 --> 00:37:28.140
No matter what, it just won't...

00:37:28.140 --> 00:37:31.810
It's here! Exwires, start reciting!

00:37:31.810 --> 00:37:33.480
What's wrong? Hurry up!

00:37:36.270 --> 00:37:37.730
Retreat!

00:37:40.480 --> 00:37:44.200
What on earth are you guys doing?!

00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:47.320
You need to get over your fear of bugs already!

00:38:01.550 --> 00:38:02.090
Hey!

00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:03.420
Hmmm?

00:38:11.350 --> 00:38:13.100
What's written here?

00:38:13.770 --> 00:38:15.520
Ah... That's nostalgic.

00:38:15.520 --> 00:38:18.600
Our dad used to read this to us when we were kids.

00:38:25.610 --> 00:38:27.450
Let's see...

00:38:31.240 --> 00:38:36.580
Long ago, a demon appeared on the outskirts of a village.

00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:42.630
The demon wasn't in good shape, so a young lad from the village fed him.

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:50.140
The demon recovered its strength, and remained in the village to play with the young lad.

00:38:50.850 --> 00:38:56.600
Because of the demon, the villagers forgot to work and spent their days in leisure.

00:38:57.310 --> 00:39:00.900
One day, an exorcist appeared, and sealed away the demon.

00:39:02.650 --> 00:39:04.440
Although the demon was taken care of,

00:39:04.440 --> 00:39:10.990
the village wasted away because the villagers had forgotten all about it.

00:39:10.990 --> 00:39:12.120
That's a lie!

00:39:12.120 --> 00:39:13.620
That's a lie! That's a lie!

00:39:14.240 --> 00:39:16.200
This is a complete lie!

00:39:16.410 --> 00:39:18.210
It's definitely wrong!

00:39:19.330 --> 00:39:21.170
What's with you all of a sudden?

00:39:23.590 --> 00:39:25.550
Don't lash out at the book.

00:39:25.550 --> 00:39:28.510
It's kinda like a memento of my dad.

00:39:31.010 --> 00:39:35.180
Is it true that the village wasted away?

00:39:35.430 --> 00:39:38.140
Uh, well, it's just a picture book.

00:40:11.260 --> 00:40:13.390
Hey! It's late, so go to sleep.

00:40:19.980 --> 00:40:21.640
You can sleep on my bed.

00:40:22.480 --> 00:40:24.150
Aren't you gonna sleep?

00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:27.650
Not yet, 'cos I totally haven't finished my assignments for today.

00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:29.900
Aren't you sleepy?

00:40:29.900 --> 00:40:32.910
I'm sleepy, but I gotta finish all this work...

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.870
So, you think it would be great if all your homework disappeared, right?

00:40:36.870 --> 00:40:38.700
Yeah, of course!

00:40:38.700 --> 00:40:42.580
So, you think it would be great if all the homework could disappear, right?

00:40:42.580 --> 00:40:45.420
Yeah... I wonder if that could happen...

00:40:50.920 --> 00:40:54.180
That's why I have to get it done as quickly as possible.

00:41:08.150 --> 00:41:09.610
I guess I'll go to bed too!

00:41:09.610 --> 00:41:11.990
Let's go to bed together!

00:41:27.040 --> 00:41:28.290
Why is it out of the cage?

00:41:38.050 --> 00:41:39.510
Nostalgic, isn't it?

00:41:40.720 --> 00:41:42.350
I'd completely forgotten about it,

00:41:42.350 --> 00:41:45.140
even though Dad used to read it to us quite a bit.

00:41:45.890 --> 00:41:47.690
Why did you let it out of the cage?

00:41:49.270 --> 00:41:51.360
Your duty is to watch it, isn't it?

00:41:51.980 --> 00:41:55.070
Anyway, today's homework, did you do it properly?

00:41:55.740 --> 00:41:56.820
Homework?

00:41:57.200 --> 00:41:58.570
As expected, you didn't...

00:41:58.570 --> 00:42:01.700
Do you understand the position you're in now that you're under house arrest?

00:42:01.700 --> 00:42:04.250
You can't watch the demon properly and you can't do your homework properly.

00:42:04.250 --> 00:42:05.580
Because of that, you're...

00:42:05.580 --> 00:42:07.170
Shut up!

00:42:09.710 --> 00:42:12.130
So it's fine if we're in the cage, right?

00:42:18.590 --> 00:42:21.680
That demon will be sealed once the festival is over.

00:42:22.260 --> 00:42:24.730
Until then, do not take your eyes off it.

00:42:28.100 --> 00:42:31.360
Seriously, what homework was he nagging about anyway?

00:42:38.360 --> 00:42:40.370
Was that the beginning?

00:42:40.370 --> 00:42:43.790
Yeah, it's a story from a thousand years ago.

00:42:44.450 --> 00:42:47.370
Anyway, if it were you, what would you do?

00:42:47.830 --> 00:42:53.460
If you met the demon from this picture book, what would you do?

00:43:01.140 --> 00:43:03.890
I would do my best to finish it off!

00:43:16.900 --> 00:43:18.610
Around two hours ago,

00:43:18.610 --> 00:43:21.990
there was a sighting of the Phantom Train at the South District.

00:43:21.990 --> 00:43:22.830
Let's get going.

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:31.460
Speaking of which, I heard from Shura-san that your family has quite a long history with this festival.

00:43:32.080 --> 00:43:36.760
My ancestor was the legendary exorcist depicted in that picture book.

00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:40.550
What's wrong? If you want an autograph, I'll give it to you later.

00:43:49.560 --> 00:43:51.310
I can't do this anymore.

00:43:51.310 --> 00:43:54.190
The MOLBs today were amazing, weren't they?

00:43:54.190 --> 00:43:56.440
By the way, why are they called MOLB?

00:43:56.440 --> 00:44:00.070
Monsters of Liquid Balloon. In short, MOLB.

00:44:00.070 --> 00:44:02.820
So, they're just water-balloon ghosts.

00:44:03.780 --> 00:44:05.030
Okumura!

00:44:05.030 --> 00:44:06.990
Can you lend us your bath?

00:44:06.990 --> 00:44:08.040
Sure!

00:44:13.380 --> 00:44:15.000
Come at me!

00:44:16.960 --> 00:44:19.720
No! Kick it with your legs!

00:44:19.720 --> 00:44:21.260
Is that okay?

00:44:21.260 --> 00:44:23.680
They're completely getting along.

00:44:24.220 --> 00:44:26.850
Hey! Okumura, what are you doing?

00:44:28.310 --> 00:44:32.190
Ah! Well, one can't be cooped up in a room all day, right?

00:44:32.190 --> 00:44:35.360
Gotta come out and play once in a while!

00:44:36.110 --> 00:44:38.530
After you're done with your bath, come and join us!

00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:45.490
Let's play ball!

00:44:45.820 --> 00:44:47.830
Why baseball?

00:44:47.830 --> 00:44:49.200
Well...

00:44:50.500 --> 00:44:53.920
If we're talking about having fun during lunch break, it's gotta be baseball!

00:44:58.550 --> 00:44:59.920
Strike!

00:45:00.300 --> 00:45:02.130
Go, Izumo!

00:45:02.130 --> 00:45:03.680
Crush them!

00:45:04.720 --> 00:45:07.100
Our hard-earned lunch break is going to waste.

00:45:12.020 --> 00:45:14.310
My hand slipped.

00:45:20.650 --> 00:45:24.200
H-He's signaling a homerun? Darn!

00:45:24.450 --> 00:45:29.200
You bastard! Do you know how fast my straights are?!

00:45:29.490 --> 00:45:30.870
What an idiot.

00:45:30.870 --> 00:45:33.120
Hey, shall the two of us just run off?

00:45:33.120 --> 00:45:35.210
Who's gonna run off with you?

00:45:35.210 --> 00:45:36.500
How uncooperative...

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:39.040
Try and hit my straight!

00:45:41.760 --> 00:45:43.720
I got it!

00:45:44.130 --> 00:45:44.880
Huh?

00:45:45.720 --> 00:45:47.970
This is way too easy.

00:45:50.970 --> 00:45:52.930
I got it.

00:45:56.810 --> 00:45:58.480
This level is way too low.

00:45:58.900 --> 00:46:01.980
Okay, Usamaro! It's your turn next!

00:46:11.910 --> 00:46:12.830
What's wrong?

00:46:12.830 --> 00:46:14.500
Ah... Nothing's...

00:46:18.170 --> 00:46:21.040
They totally look like they're having fun.

00:46:21.630 --> 00:46:23.050
It's an eyesore.

00:46:23.050 --> 00:46:25.050
We should get rid of it before it becomes a problem.

00:46:25.420 --> 00:46:26.260
What?

00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:27.720
But Lord Pheles said...

00:46:28.430 --> 00:46:30.680
Why are you sympathizing with a demon?

00:46:31.100 --> 00:46:33.470
An exorcist's job is to exorcise demons!

00:46:38.230 --> 00:46:39.440
I know that.

00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:42.320
Do you get it?

00:46:42.320 --> 00:46:44.690
Swing with all you've got!

00:46:46.740 --> 00:46:49.410
It'd be better if you grip it a little lower.

00:46:51.700 --> 00:46:53.910
Yup, that's it. Around there.

00:46:53.910 --> 00:46:55.750
When the ball comes, swing it forward.

00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:04.670
Don't worry about it! That was a good swing! Just do it again!

00:47:04.670 --> 00:47:06.880
I won't go easy on you just 'cuz you're a kid!

00:47:06.880 --> 00:47:09.130
Give it your all! Hit it really hard!

00:47:15.470 --> 00:47:17.020
Run to first base.

00:47:20.100 --> 00:47:22.310
Usamaro! Over here!

00:47:23.570 --> 00:47:26.150
Ah, you can leave the bat here.

00:47:29.490 --> 00:47:30.950
Over here!

00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:32.120
Bon, you threw it too hard!

00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:33.830
Just shut up!

00:47:34.830 --> 00:47:37.830
You did it, Usamaro! That's a homerun with bases loaded!

00:47:37.830 --> 00:47:40.120
H-Homerun?

00:47:40.120 --> 00:47:43.590
That was amazing, Usamaro-kun!

00:49:36.490 --> 00:49:39.330
So, it's just another piece of it. A dead end, huh?

00:49:40.950 --> 00:49:42.080
I'll be back in a minute.

00:49:42.080 --> 00:49:43.000
What's up?

00:49:43.370 --> 00:49:47.000
The rubble over that demon's small shrine is being cleared up, so I have to go supervise that.

00:50:00.470 --> 00:50:01.970
It stinks...

00:50:01.970 --> 00:50:02.890
My apologies!

00:50:02.890 --> 00:50:05.020
It seems like the pump isn't working properly.

00:50:05.020 --> 00:50:07.480
But the water level's been rising steadily since just now.

00:50:07.480 --> 00:50:09.190
Is everything all right?

00:50:09.190 --> 00:50:12.030
Please finish up before everything becomes submerged!

00:50:12.030 --> 00:50:14.150
What the hell <i>is</i> this? Damn it.

00:50:14.150 --> 00:50:17.570
Mephisto, that bastard. He's failing to manage this properly.

00:50:21.410 --> 00:50:23.330
Thank you for the food!

00:50:25.210 --> 00:50:28.080
Usamaro-kun's able to say that properly now.

00:50:28.750 --> 00:50:30.420
He's... really cute!

00:50:30.420 --> 00:50:35.420
Usamaro-kun, if you're this cute, why were you sealed away?

00:50:35.420 --> 00:50:36.630
I don't know.

00:50:36.930 --> 00:50:38.930
He doesn't seem to have any memories.

00:50:38.930 --> 00:50:41.560
With the festival right in front of our eyes,

00:50:41.560 --> 00:50:43.600
it kills me that we still have to work.

00:50:43.600 --> 00:50:45.270
Quit complaining.

00:50:45.270 --> 00:50:48.060
We still have patrol duty in District One tonight.

00:50:48.060 --> 00:50:49.940
That was the day before.

00:50:49.940 --> 00:50:51.610
It's District Six tonight.

00:50:51.610 --> 00:50:52.940
That was yesterday.

00:50:53.190 --> 00:50:55.240
Bon, I guess you're totally out of it too, huh?

00:50:55.240 --> 00:50:59.860
You're the one who couldn't remember what you wanted at the convenience store and came back empty handed.

00:50:59.860 --> 00:51:02.240
When did we go to the convenience store?

00:51:02.740 --> 00:51:05.080
You can't come in here.

00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:13.670
Did you...?

00:51:13.670 --> 00:51:15.840
The entomophobic Shima-san just...

00:51:16.550 --> 00:51:17.720
Somethin' wrong with ya?

00:51:17.720 --> 00:51:20.050
Maybe you should take the day off!

00:51:20.050 --> 00:51:21.430
What's wrong?

00:51:22.600 --> 00:51:25.270
Those guys are getting pretty worked up.

00:51:24.930 --> 00:51:26.310
What's wrong with the three of you?

00:51:26.310 --> 00:51:29.140
Oh, Shiemi? What happened? You've got a bandage.

00:51:29.140 --> 00:51:29.890
What?

00:51:30.560 --> 00:51:33.440
Did you fall or something? Be careful!

00:51:39.110 --> 00:51:43.200
Oh, no! I need to experience more of the festival! Give me the festival!

00:51:43.200 --> 00:51:45.620
Give me festival!

00:51:46.080 --> 00:51:48.120
Does everyone want to go to the festival?

00:51:48.120 --> 00:51:51.630
Well, if everyone didn't have work to do, we'd want to go.

00:51:52.170 --> 00:51:55.380
So if you didn't have work, you could all go to the festival?

00:51:55.630 --> 00:51:56.840
Of course.

00:51:56.840 --> 00:52:00.130
If people didn't have work, then
everyone in town would participate!

00:52:00.720 --> 00:52:03.760
Does everyone in town think that way?

00:52:03.760 --> 00:52:07.270
I'm sure they do! It's everyone's wish.

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:34.920
What's wrong?

00:52:35.460 --> 00:52:39.300
I've been trying to get in touch with HQ, but no one's picking up.

00:52:48.720 --> 00:52:50.060
There it is.

00:52:57.900 --> 00:52:59.030
That's...

00:54:34.160 --> 00:54:37.750
Here ye, here ye. The legendary exorcist has arrived!

00:54:38.750 --> 00:54:41.000
I've been waiting for you, you giant rabbit.

00:54:41.000 --> 00:54:43.380
Now is the time for our battle!

00:55:05.490 --> 00:55:07.320
What's everyone doing?!

00:55:07.570 --> 00:55:09.570
What, you ask? It's obvious, isn't it?

00:55:09.910 --> 00:55:13.330
What are you doing away from your posts? What happened to your mission?

00:55:13.660 --> 00:55:15.040
Mission?

00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:16.830
You mean this?

00:55:17.540 --> 00:55:20.750
No! There should've been a patrol mission!

00:55:20.750 --> 00:55:23.000
I haven't heard of anything like that.

00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:23.800
What?

00:55:23.800 --> 00:55:28.090
Oh, Okumura-sensei! How would you like to try one of these?

00:55:28.090 --> 00:55:31.090
Where have you been, Okumura-sensei?

00:55:31.430 --> 00:55:33.220
Are you injured? What happened to your arm?

00:55:34.510 --> 00:55:37.930
Even the teachers are here. What on earth is going on?

00:55:43.900 --> 00:55:45.780
Impossible! How on earth did it get past the barrier?!

00:55:46.610 --> 00:55:47.780
What's that?

00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:50.320
That's rare. It's a MOLB.

00:55:50.990 --> 00:55:53.120
This is my first time seeing one. Wait! It's heading this way!

00:55:57.120 --> 00:55:57.950
Shit...

00:56:05.040 --> 00:56:07.010
What the heck is this?!

00:56:07.010 --> 00:56:08.880
Usamaro!

00:56:18.890 --> 00:56:21.640
Rin! Where are you?

00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:25.440
Rin!

00:56:27.320 --> 00:56:29.440
Where did you go?

00:56:29.440 --> 00:56:31.110
Huh?

00:56:31.110 --> 00:56:33.280
Shiratori-san, do you know him?

00:56:33.280 --> 00:56:34.240
Nope.

00:56:34.240 --> 00:56:36.830
The man of the year defeated the big rabbit!

00:56:36.830 --> 00:56:38.290
Let's go!

00:56:46.290 --> 00:56:47.840
Are you all right, boy?

00:56:47.840 --> 00:56:49.510
Where are your mom and dad?

00:56:52.840 --> 00:56:53.930
Are you alone?

00:56:54.260 --> 00:56:56.180
Boy, what's your name?

00:56:56.180 --> 00:56:57.890
Can you tell me where you live?

00:57:01.480 --> 00:57:05.360
What're you doing? Don't wander off on your own.

00:57:05.360 --> 00:57:06.190
Rin!

00:57:07.400 --> 00:57:09.820
Thank goodness, looks like he's not a lost child.

00:57:11.030 --> 00:57:12.610
Let's go back to where everyone else is.

00:57:49.690 --> 00:57:54.530
When the festival is over, will I be sealed again?

00:58:00.030 --> 00:58:03.250
Leave it to me. I'll do something about it.

00:58:22.470 --> 00:58:26.060
This brings back memories. I was here 11 years ago too.

00:58:26.060 --> 00:58:29.060
At that time, Yukio got lost,

00:58:29.060 --> 00:58:32.070
and our Dad and I were searching for him around here.

00:58:32.320 --> 00:58:36.070
In the end, he was crying alone on the shrine grounds.

00:58:36.450 --> 00:58:42.040
The moment he saw me and Dad, he was so relieved that he started wailing.

00:58:49.330 --> 00:58:51.210
Is it something sad?

00:58:51.960 --> 00:58:53.130
What're you saying?

00:58:53.130 --> 00:58:54.630
Is it something painful?

00:58:54.630 --> 00:58:56.470
There's no way it's p—

00:59:39.050 --> 00:59:44.220
Memories... of Dad... are painful.

00:59:54.650 --> 00:59:55.900
Isn't that...?

00:59:56.570 --> 00:59:57.740
Who's there?

00:59:58.320 --> 00:59:59.740
Is someone there?

01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:01.360
Um...

01:00:01.820 --> 01:00:02.910
There he is!

01:00:02.910 --> 01:00:03.990
Yukio!

01:00:03.990 --> 01:00:07.250
Dad! Read us this book!

01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.460
It's us when we were young...

01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.460
Again?

01:00:09.460 --> 01:00:11.670
Please. It's good, isn't it?

01:00:10.000 --> 01:00:11.170
Yukio's here too...

01:00:11.670 --> 01:00:13.250
But who's that?

01:00:12.380 --> 01:00:14.960
Looks like you guys really like this book.

01:00:14.960 --> 01:00:18.920
I can't remember but I have feeling he was someone really important.

01:00:16.000 --> 01:00:17.260
Okay, okay. I will.

01:00:19.840 --> 01:00:22.260
What's wrong, Rin?

01:00:24.010 --> 01:00:24.970
Dad...

01:00:27.060 --> 01:00:28.310
Dad!

01:00:40.530 --> 01:00:42.660
This is...

01:00:44.660 --> 01:00:48.240
So you remembered the memories I took so much trouble to eat...

01:00:48.240 --> 01:00:51.870
Don't tell me... it was you who ate those memories?

01:00:52.420 --> 01:00:56.790
I'll eat all those unpleasant or painful memories.

01:00:57.210 --> 01:01:00.800
This was the reason you were sealed?!

01:01:01.050 --> 01:01:04.300
It'll be all right, Rin. I'll eat them all again.

01:01:07.430 --> 01:01:08.850
Stop it!

01:01:20.110 --> 01:01:21.110
Usamaro?

01:01:21.440 --> 01:01:23.610
So you finally show your true form, Rabbit.

01:01:23.610 --> 01:01:27.450
To think I'd meet a "Turner of Time" in a place like this.

01:01:27.450 --> 01:01:30.040
In the name of my ancestors, I'll seal you!

01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:34.040
What do you think you're doing?

01:01:36.920 --> 01:01:40.550
You bastard. You don't have what it takes to be an exorcist after all!

01:02:31.180 --> 01:02:32.600
What happened to our backup?!

01:02:32.600 --> 01:02:34.520
What's HQ doing?!

01:02:35.180 --> 01:02:38.190
It's because of that demon. At this rate...

01:02:43.730 --> 01:02:46.530
What on earth is that rabbit?

01:02:47.070 --> 01:02:49.280
It's the Turner of Time.

01:02:49.280 --> 01:02:51.700
It manipulates time and eats people's memories.

01:02:52.870 --> 01:02:55.450
It's the demon that my ancestors once sealed.

01:02:56.250 --> 01:02:59.330
It takes advantage of the smallest desires,

01:02:59.330 --> 01:03:01.750
and has the power to destroy people's hearts.

01:03:02.460 --> 01:03:06.920
Because my ancestor allowed that demon to dwell with the villagers,

01:03:06.920 --> 01:03:09.760
the village was brought to ruin.

01:03:10.390 --> 01:03:13.060
The village and the location where the demon was sealed was forgotten over time

01:03:13.470 --> 01:03:15.730
and became a myth.

01:03:16.310 --> 01:03:19.810
If we leave him alone, this town will be destroyed as well.

01:03:57.520 --> 01:03:58.520
How'd it go?

01:03:58.520 --> 01:03:59.730
Nothing yet.

01:04:01.270 --> 01:04:02.980
Yes! We haven't found anything yet.

01:04:02.980 --> 01:04:04.520
In the western side?

01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:10.780
Understood. We're heading over there.

01:04:11.450 --> 01:04:12.410
Nii-sa—

01:04:19.750 --> 01:04:20.870
Why?

01:04:21.420 --> 01:04:25.380
When everyone forgets their unpleasant memories, they become happy!

01:04:25.380 --> 01:04:26.340
So why...

01:04:44.440 --> 01:04:47.440
No! There must be some mistake!

01:04:51.950 --> 01:04:54.530
No... I didn't do anything.

01:04:55.870 --> 01:04:56.990
No...

01:05:02.460 --> 01:05:05.840
Hey! Can you hear me? Hang in there!

01:05:07.710 --> 01:05:11.090
No...

01:05:33.740 --> 01:05:34.610
Rin...

01:05:39.160 --> 01:05:40.740
Which way did they go?

01:05:42.790 --> 01:05:44.290
Shall we split up?

01:05:46.750 --> 01:05:47.750
An earthquake?

01:05:48.540 --> 01:05:50.920
This aura... It's the demon!

01:06:02.520 --> 01:06:04.060
Ouch!

01:06:11.610 --> 01:06:13.320
What <i>is</i> this place?

01:06:14.530 --> 01:06:15.150
Nii-san!

01:06:15.150 --> 01:06:15.740
Hold it.

01:06:16.200 --> 01:06:17.160
Look.

01:06:27.210 --> 01:06:29.170
Don't take your eyes off that rabbit!

01:06:49.940 --> 01:06:52.610
Even if it's you, Rin, I hate exorcists!

01:06:52.860 --> 01:06:55.610
Usamaro, why are you eating people's memories?

01:06:55.860 --> 01:06:59.780
Forgetting unpleasant things makes everyone look happy!

01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:00.620
And yet...!

01:07:00.820 --> 01:07:03.870
Even if you eat one person's memories, someone else will remember too, right?

01:07:03.870 --> 01:07:06.500
So, I'll eat that person's memories too!

01:07:06.500 --> 01:07:09.920
There are lots of people in this town.
Are you gonna eat everyone's memories?

01:07:09.920 --> 01:07:17.880
Whether it's a town, or a country, I'll eat and eat and eat everyone's memories! And then everyone will become happy!

01:07:18.130 --> 01:07:20.640
Even the memories you and I share?

01:07:20.640 --> 01:07:22.010
That...

01:07:24.680 --> 01:07:26.600
No matter what you say to it, you're just wasting your breath.

01:07:26.600 --> 01:07:27.640
Nii-san, you stand back!

01:07:27.640 --> 01:07:30.230
Hold on, Yukio. Usamaro, I—

01:07:40.820 --> 01:07:41.870
Yukio!

01:08:12.100 --> 01:08:13.560
Hold on, you guys!

01:09:28.720 --> 01:09:30.100
Usamaro!

01:09:34.230 --> 01:09:36.150
Let go of me, Rin!

01:09:36.480 --> 01:09:41.190
Usamaro, you used that power because you wanted to make everyone happy, right?

01:09:41.440 --> 01:09:43.950
That's right! And yet...! Yet...!

01:09:44.410 --> 01:09:46.950
In that case, you're a good guy.

01:09:47.990 --> 01:09:49.080
Rin...

01:09:54.500 --> 01:09:55.790
But you know, Usamaro,

01:09:55.790 --> 01:09:59.090
no matter how painful or sad some things are,

01:09:59.090 --> 01:10:01.090
there are things you must not forget.

01:10:01.510 --> 01:10:04.510
No matter how painful my memories of me and dad are,

01:10:04.510 --> 01:10:07.850
I won't forget them! I must never forget them!

01:10:15.850 --> 01:10:21.110
Don't you think that true memories are a
combination of fun ones and painful ones?

01:10:24.110 --> 01:10:24.990
Nii-san...

01:10:36.370 --> 01:10:37.500
Rin...

01:11:25.380 --> 01:11:28.550
That's why, Usamaro, promise me.

01:11:28.550 --> 01:11:30.590
Don't ever eat people's memories again.

01:11:31.300 --> 01:11:33.680
Don't ever use that power again.

01:11:35.350 --> 01:11:36.100
Okay.

01:11:38.310 --> 01:11:39.190
Yukio!

01:11:41.020 --> 01:11:43.690
I'll take this guy in and make him our little brother.

01:11:45.570 --> 01:11:47.240
I've been thinking about this for a while.

01:11:47.240 --> 01:11:51.820
Dad knew I was a half-demon and still raised me.

01:11:52.320 --> 01:11:55.330
So from today, the three of us will be brothers!

01:11:56.290 --> 01:11:57.830
What on earth are you saying, Nii-san!

01:11:58.330 --> 01:12:00.750
I'll explain everything to Mephisto.

01:12:00.750 --> 01:12:02.420
That's not the problem!

01:12:17.850 --> 01:12:19.180
It's being eaten...

01:12:20.100 --> 01:12:21.600
Rin!

01:12:21.940 --> 01:12:24.610
Thank goodness! You found Usamaro-kun!

01:12:27.070 --> 01:12:28.610
What's going on? How's the barrier?

01:12:29.150 --> 01:12:31.610
They're putting the last seal in place.

01:12:31.610 --> 01:12:34.990
Anyway, an order to evacuate has been issued!

01:12:34.990 --> 01:12:38.410
A huge amount of coal tar has invaded the town and it's a mess!

01:12:38.410 --> 01:12:40.790
All exorcists are to gather at HQ!

01:13:13.200 --> 01:13:14.950
You're the oldest, so don't cry, okay?

01:13:26.500 --> 01:13:27.960
Some kids are being left behind...

01:13:28.420 --> 01:13:29.460
You guys go on ahead!

01:13:29.460 --> 01:13:30.920
Wait! I'm going with you!

01:13:30.920 --> 01:13:31.970
Rin!

01:13:32.720 --> 01:13:36.470
I'll be fine, Usamaro! I'll be back soon, so go with Shiemi, okay?

01:13:37.390 --> 01:13:39.720
Don't make such a sad face!

01:13:39.970 --> 01:13:41.390
Shiemi, I'm counting on you.

01:13:43.850 --> 01:13:45.480
Come on. Let's go.

01:13:57.030 --> 01:13:59.160
What are the guys on the outside doing?!

01:13:59.160 --> 01:14:01.910
They're eating into the barriers!

01:14:09.540 --> 01:14:10.920
The Aria team has...!

01:14:10.920 --> 01:14:12.590
Shura-san!

01:14:37.450 --> 01:14:38.450
You're late, baldy!

01:14:39.370 --> 01:14:43.160
It's not "baldy". It's Arthur Auguste Angel.

01:14:43.750 --> 01:14:47.370
I'll hold them off here. Continue your chanting!

01:14:47.370 --> 01:14:49.670
Shut up! Don't try to act all cool.

01:15:09.480 --> 01:15:12.230
Usamaro-kun, it's dangerous out here, so let's go inside.

01:15:12.900 --> 01:15:15.440
Nii-chan, could you give me some Una-una-kun?

01:15:28.330 --> 01:15:29.880
Usamaro-kun! Don't!

01:15:43.470 --> 01:15:44.600
Rin!

01:16:03.370 --> 01:16:04.330
Nii-chan!

01:16:04.330 --> 01:16:05.790
Wait right there.

01:16:11.250 --> 01:16:12.460
It's all right now.

01:16:48.620 --> 01:16:50.710
The town is...

01:17:03.470 --> 01:17:05.470
Go as far inside as you can and hide!

01:17:06.260 --> 01:17:06.680
Yukio!

01:17:11.730 --> 01:17:12.640
Damn it!

01:17:49.140 --> 01:17:50.180
Usamaro?

01:17:53.600 --> 01:17:55.350
What're you doing?! Get back!

01:17:55.650 --> 01:17:56.940
Rin!

01:17:57.440 --> 01:18:00.400
I won't forget them either!

01:18:00.400 --> 01:18:02.780
The memories I have with you!

01:18:04.360 --> 01:18:06.870
But I'm sorry.

01:18:07.320 --> 01:18:09.990
I can't keep our promise.

01:18:19.130 --> 01:18:21.130
What is he planning on doing?

01:18:36.140 --> 01:18:37.190
This is...!

01:18:37.190 --> 01:18:41.900
Not just memories... he's eating space and time itself.

01:19:04.630 --> 01:19:07.880
The bath, the baseball game, that delicious food, and the festival...

01:19:07.880 --> 01:19:10.010
They were all really fun.

01:19:11.430 --> 01:19:13.560
Thank you, Rin.

01:19:30.950 --> 01:19:32.620
What would you do, Rin?

01:19:33.700 --> 01:19:36.750
If you met the demon from this picture book...?

01:19:42.960 --> 01:19:44.210
I'd make friends with it!

01:19:44.420 --> 01:19:45.340
What?!

01:19:45.710 --> 01:19:49.380
Well, this guy was having fun with everyone, right?

01:19:49.380 --> 01:19:50.970
So he's a friend, isn't he?

01:19:51.390 --> 01:19:54.220
Friend? Nii-san, it's a demon!

01:19:54.220 --> 01:19:56.730
If it's a friend, I won't finish it off! We must make friends with it!

01:19:56.730 --> 01:20:01.600
B-But even though you become friends with it, a demon is a demon.

01:20:01.600 --> 01:20:04.020
If we can get along, even a demon can become our friend!

01:20:04.020 --> 01:20:05.480
Therefore, it's a good demon!

01:20:05.900 --> 01:20:08.280
Dad, which is the right answer?

01:20:08.610 --> 01:20:09.650
I wonder myself.

01:20:16.330 --> 01:20:17.370
Usamaro!

01:20:18.000 --> 01:20:18.710
Huh?

01:20:26.760 --> 01:20:27.880
I'm back.

01:20:28.210 --> 01:20:30.380
Yukio! Where's Usamaro! And everyone...?

01:20:30.380 --> 01:20:31.260
What happened to the town?

01:20:32.590 --> 01:20:35.430
Usamaro? Are you talking in your sleep, Nii-san?

01:20:35.760 --> 01:20:39.020
The festival's already over, so from today, please mend your ways...

01:20:41.140 --> 01:20:43.360
He ate everything...

01:20:43.360 --> 01:20:44.020
"He"?

01:20:44.810 --> 01:20:46.270
Don't you remember?

01:20:46.570 --> 01:20:48.110
What are you talking about?

01:20:54.240 --> 01:20:57.240
Okumura, what's wrong? You're all flustered.

01:20:57.240 --> 01:21:00.330
You guys... Ah, never mind.

01:21:00.330 --> 01:21:01.460
Rin?

01:21:22.810 --> 01:21:26.820
Due to a low pressure front building up since last night...

01:21:33.320 --> 01:21:36.530
Usamaro!

01:21:56.760 --> 01:21:58.600
Do you remember?

01:21:59.930 --> 01:22:05.730
If you have memories no one else remembers, what's the point in remembering them?

01:22:07.900 --> 01:22:09.610
Or something like that.

01:22:09.610 --> 01:22:12.690
Having the power to open a demon's heart...

01:22:12.690 --> 01:22:15.110
You've shown me something interesting.

01:22:25.750 --> 01:22:26.620
Ah...

01:22:44.310 --> 01:22:46.940
Usamaro, I won't forget.

01:22:46.940 --> 01:22:48.270
I'll always remember.

01:23:09.290 --> 01:23:14.510
Brother, the ending in this book is different.

01:23:15.340 --> 01:23:20.930
I didn't like that ending very much, but he rewrote it anyway.

01:23:36.110 --> 01:23:36.820
Oh?

01:23:37.700 --> 01:23:40.110
Where did you suddenly run off to?

01:23:40.110 --> 01:23:42.030
Oh, shut up.

01:23:42.030 --> 01:23:45.040
Even <i>I</i> have times when I just wanna think alone, you know?

01:23:45.040 --> 01:23:46.450
Think?

01:23:46.450 --> 01:23:50.580
Anyway, Nii-san, the only thing you <i>should</i> be thinking of is your homework.

01:23:47.790 --> 01:23:50.580
Listen, tempt providence.

01:23:50.580 --> 01:23:54.130
Homework, homework! Are you my mom or something?

01:23:54.090 --> 01:23:56.210
Kessen lock on rip up

01:23:54.090 --> 01:23:56.210
Final battle! Lock on, rip up.

01:23:54.590 --> 01:23:58.220
Anyway, are you hungry? I'll make some omu-rice!

01:24:09.190 --> 01:24:11.100
Listen, tempt providence.

01:24:11.230 --> 01:24:12.860
Final battle! Lock on, rip up.

01:24:13.270 --> 01:24:16.320
Sound, we'll make you listen to our page.

01:24:16.480 --> 01:24:18.240
There are countless worlds you've never seen.

01:24:18.530 --> 01:24:21.320
Follow never never! Next next next next, yeah!

01:24:21.360 --> 01:24:29.500
With those hands, if you could change the color of anything,

01:24:29.660 --> 01:24:35.670
what color would you change it to?

01:24:36.250 --> 01:24:41.970
From a way of life born from anxiety and confusion,

01:24:42.260 --> 01:24:44.680
I try my best to find relief.

01:24:45.180 --> 01:24:49.680
While holding my breath in this filthy world,

01:24:49.770 --> 01:24:54.190
had I gotten comfortable joining the masses of adults betrayed during their youth?

01:24:54.190 --> 01:24:56.770
Reversi, we'll make you lose with our win.

01:24:57.150 --> 01:24:58.990
There are countless world you've never seen

01:24:59.240 --> 01:25:02.160
Follow never never! Next next next next, yeah!

01:25:02.160 --> 01:25:06.450
I reach out countless times in this shackled society.

01:25:06.450 --> 01:25:10.460
But this wasn't what I was trying to grasp.

01:25:10.620 --> 01:25:14.750
Running away only brings about your own happiness in this world.

01:25:14.960 --> 01:25:18.960
Because we can say we're still not here.

01:25:19.090 --> 01:25:27.470
With those hands, if you could change the color of anything,

01:25:27.600 --> 01:25:33.560
you would paint the indecision in my heart black and white.

01:25:45.530 --> 01:25:47.240
Listen, tempt providence.

01:25:47.240 --> 01:25:49.200
Final battle! Lock on, rip up.

01:25:49.200 --> 01:25:57.590
As my friends achieved their dreams, I felt myself die bit by bit.

01:25:58.000 --> 01:26:00.340
What did I try to protect?

01:26:00.340 --> 01:26:07.100
If I lost it, would I really be troubled, even though I haven't reached it?

01:26:07.100 --> 01:26:09.760
Reversi, we'll make you lose with our win.

